DejaVuSans.ttf and DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf are from the DejaVu Fonts project
(https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/), used here to render the build-time social
share cards (generate/share-card.ts) via satori.

The DejaVu fonts are released under a free license (derived from the Bitstream
Vera Fonts license) that permits redistribution and bundling. Full text:
https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/License.html

They are vendored (committed) rather than read from the system so the build is
reproducible on any machine / CI. satori requires STATIC font instances — it
cannot parse variable fonts — which is why two static weights are shipped
rather than a single variable file. To swap in a different typeface, drop in
its static Regular/Bold .ttf files and update loadFonts() + the fontFamily in
generate/share-card.ts.
